<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
    <head>
        <%
        const formatGuideExportValues = (Array.isArray(exportFormats) ? exportFormats : [])
            .map((format) => String(format?.value || '').trim().toLowerCase())
            .filter(Boolean);
        const formatGuideLegacyExportsEnabled = formatGuideExportValues.some((value) => value !== 'ltd');
        const formatGuideQrExportsEnabled = formatGuideExportValues.includes('qr');
        const pageTitle = 'Mii File Format Guide - InfiniMii';
        const pageDesc = 'Reference guide to common Mii file formats, QR workflows, compatibility notes, and which InfiniMii tools to use for each format.';
        const canonicalUrl = `${baseUrl}/guides/formats`;
        const keywords = 'mii file formats, mii format guide, wii mii file, 3ds mii format, switch mii data, mii qr format';
        const breadcrumbs = [
            { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
            { name: 'Mii Format Guide', url: '/guides/formats' }
        ];
        const schemaType = 'TechArticle';
        %>
        <%- include('metaTags', { title: pageTitle, description: pageDesc, canonicalUrl, keywords }) %>
        <%- include('structuredData') %>
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/global.css">
        <link rel="stylesheet" href="/utilityPages.css">
    </head>
    <body>
        <%- include('globalStyle') %>
        <%- include('header') %>
        <%- include('accountDisplay') %>
        <main class="content faq-content" role="main">
            <%- include('sidebar') %>
            <article class="faq-article">
                <h1>Mii File Format Guide</h1>
                <p class="faq-lede">A quick reference for the Mii formats you will run into on InfiniMii, what each one is for, and which tool to use next.</p>

                <nav class="faq-nav" aria-label="Format Guide Sections">
                    <h2>Browse this guide</h2>
                    <ul class="faq-nav-list">
                        <li><a href="#formats">Common Mii Formats</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#tools">Which Tool Should You Use?</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#compatibility">Compatibility Notes</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </nav>

                <section id="formats" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Common Mii Formats</h2>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <ul>
                            <li><strong>Wii-era formats:</strong> <code>RCD</code> and <code>RSD</code> are Nintendo's names for classic Wii-era Mii files. You may also see <code>MII</code>, <code>MIIGX</code>, or <code>MAE</code>. These names came from separate reverse-engineering projects and generally refer to RCD data.</li>
                            <li><strong>3DS and Wii U formats:</strong> <code>CFCD</code>, <code>CFSD</code>, <code>FFCD</code>, and <code>FFSD</code> store Mii data used by these systems. <code>CFED</code> and <code>FFED</code> are community names for the encrypted forms used in QR codes. PNG, JPG, and other image files can carry QR codes for compatible tools, 3DS, and Wii U.</li>
                            <li><strong>QR:</strong> <%= formatGuideQrExportsEnabled
                                ? 'Choose the QR export for a scannable code used by a compatible system such as 3DS or Wii U.'
                                : 'QR output is not available for the selected Living the Dream Mii. Its original download format is LTD.' %></li>
                            <li><strong>Modern formats:</strong> <code>NFCD</code>, <code>NFSD</code>, and <code>charinfo</code> cover newer Nintendo Mii data workflows.</li>
                            <li><strong>LTD:</strong> InfiniMii keeps original LTD files unchanged. Living the Dream Miis stay LTD-only, while Miis from other systems can use the compatible export formats listed here.</li>
                            <li><strong>My Nintendo Mii Studio:</strong> <code>MNMS</code> is stored in the Mii Studio website's local storage. Copy it as hexadecimal data to use it with compatible import and export tools.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section id="tools" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Which Tool Should You Use?</h2>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <ul>
                            <li>Use the <a href="/miiDashboard">Mii Dashboard</a> when you already have Mii data and need a preview, JSON editing, recreation instructions, or <%= formatGuideLegacyExportsEnabled ? 'one of the listed output formats' : 'an LTD download' %><%= formatGuideQrExportsEnabled ? ', including a QR code' : '' %>.</li>
                            <li><a href="/qr">QR Scanner</a> when you are starting from a QR image.</li>
                            <li><a href="/guides/transfer">Transfer Guide</a> when the best method depends on the source and destination hardware.</li>
                            <li><a href="/amiibo">Amiibo extraction</a> or <a href="/wiimote">Wii Remote Tools</a> when your Mii lives inside those specific devices.</li>
                        </ul>
                        <p><a href="/miiDashboard" class="cta-link">Open the Mii Dashboard</a></p>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section id="compatibility" class="faq-section">
                    <h2>Compatibility Notes</h2>
                    <div class="faq-item">
                        <% if (!formatGuideLegacyExportsEnabled) { %>
                            <p><strong>LTD compatibility:</strong> a Living the Dream Mii keeps its original LTD download instead of being converted to an older format.</p>
                        <% } %>
                        <ul>
                            <li>Older Nintendo systems support fewer facial features than newer ones, so converting for an older system can simplify some details.</li>
                            <li>QR code workflows are especially useful for 3DS and Wii U transfers.</li>
                            <li>Switch-related transfers often rely on manual recreation or Amiibo instead of direct file import.</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </section>
            </article>
            <%- include('featuredMiis') %>
        </main>
        <%- include('footer') %>
    </body>
</html>
